 "note": "Box-out contest ON by default (2026-09-23), TWO-DIRECTIONAL as built. When a defensive crasher has an offensive crasher within BOXOUT_PAIR_RADIUS 8.0, the two contest the box-out - score (0.4*RB + 0.4*ST + 0.1*IQ + 0.1*CH) x randint(1,6), a tie to the defender - and the LOSER's crash destination is pushed back away from the rim by BOXOUT_PUSHBACK_FRACTION 0.5 of his remaining travel. Either side can lose: the defender won 48.3% of 8,792 contests. Nothing retuned; the flip moved a default, not a number. BOTH footings move and every seed differs in all four cells - the box-out is scheme-independent (it keys on crasher geometry, not on man vs zone), so SD=0 moves like SD=1. Team-level rebounding does NOT move: at n=120 seed-paired, OREB -0.36 +-1.27, DREB -0.53 +-1.49, OREB share -0.42 +-1.59, and no metric clears its CI, while per-player P(rebound|winner) is 1.69x P(rebound|loser). Reproduce the superseded reference with GOB_BOXOUT_CONTEST=0 (verified 40/40 on fp AND draws, all four cells, every counter at zero, before the re-cut). See reports/boxout-flip-2026-09-23.md.",
